\ hello-2x2.ga - print a greeting on the serial port of node 100, on the
\ chip that examples/chips/2x2.zon describes, as uart.ga does on node 708
\ of a GA144:
\
\     gasim run --chip examples/chips/2x2.zon --uart 100 examples/chips/hello-2x2.ga

node 100
: main
    io b!                  \ B addresses io, to drive pin 1
    'message a!            \ A walks through the message
    @+ for @+ send next    \ the first word is the length - 1
    right a! @             \ wait forever on node 101

\ drives pin 1 high (3) or low (2) for a bit: 429 unexts of 2.4 ns each,
\ and the code around them
: bit ( level ) !b 428 for unext ;

\ a start bit, 8 data bits from the lowest, and a stop bit, inverted
: send ( c )
    3 bit
    7 for dup 1 and 1 xor 2 + bit 2/ next drop
    2 bit ;

: message 13 , "Hello, world!" 10 ,
